The Ten Commandments in a new interpretation for the present time by Abd-ru-shin, the author of the Grail Message - In the Light of Truth. The interpretations are reproduced in the original without commentary and in full.



The 9th Commandment:


Do not covet your neighbor's wife!


This commandment is sharply and clearly directed against the physical-animal instincts which man ... unfortunately ... often allows to arise as soon as he has the opportunity!


This also touches on the crucial point, which is the biggest pitfall for people, and which almost all of them fall victim to as soon as they come into contact with it: opportunity!


The drive is only awakened and guided by thoughts! People can easily observe that the drive does not move, cannot move, if there are no thoughts! They are completely dependent on it! Without exception!


Do not say that the sense of touch can also awaken desire; for that is false. It is only an illusion. The sense of touch only awakens the thought, and this then awakens the desire! And to awaken thoughts, the opportunity that presents itself is the most powerful tool that people must fear!


For this reason, however, it is also the greatest defense and the greatest protection for all people of both sexes if the opportunity for this is avoided! It is the lifeline in the present emergency, until the whole of humanity has become so strong within itself that it is able to keep the hearth of its thoughts pure as a matter of course . Then a violation of the commandment is absolutely impossible.


Many storms must sweep over humanity in a cleansing manner until then, but the anchor will hold if every striver makes a rigorous effort never to give the opportunity for the seductive solitude of both sexes!


Let everyone imprint this on themselves with the writing of fire; for it is not so easy to free oneself spiritually from the transgression, since the other side is also involved! And there is only rarely a possibility of simultaneous ascension.


"Do not covet your neighbor's wife!" This does not only mean a wife, but the female sex in general! This includes daughters! And since it is clearly stated: "Do not covet! ", this only refers to physical desire, not to honest courtship!


There can be no error in these clear words. This is about the strict divine law against seduction or rape, as well as against defilement through the thoughts of a secret desire! This, as the starting point of the full evil of an act, is already a transgression of the commandment, which brings punishment through karma, which must inevitably be triggered in some way before the soul can be free of it again.


Sometimes this event, which people mistakenly regard as a small thing, is even decisive for the type of next incarnation on earth or for their future fate in this earthly existence. Therefore, do not take the power of thoughts too lightly, which naturally also carries responsibility to the same extent! You are liable for even the smallest careless thought, for it causes damage in the subtle world - the world that has to receive you after this earthly life.


But if the desire even reaches the point of seduction, that is, of a gross material act, then fear retribution if you are no longer able to make amends physically and mentally on earth!


Whether the seduction is carried out in the most flattering way or in a strict demand, even if the female side finally agrees, the reciprocal effect cannot be deterred by this, it has already started with the desire, and all wisdom, all arts contribute to intensifying it. The final consent does not cancel it out!


Therefore, be on your guard, avoid every opportunity and do not give in to carelessness! First and foremost, keep the hearth of your thoughts pure! Then you will never violate this commandment!


It is also no excuse if a person tries to deceive himself into believing that the marriage was probable! Because that would be a gross untruth.


A marriage without soul love is not valid before God. But soul love remains the best protection against the violation of the commandment, since a truly loving person always wants only the best for the other person he loves and can therefore never make impure wishes or demands, which are what the commandment is primarily directed against!


